source @arxiv/math/mesland-2013
source @arxiv/math/bertozzini-conti-lewkeeratiyutkul-2006
source @arxiv/family-therapy/tomm-1987
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972

# === The agent_triple carrier ===
#
# Typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the four
# constituents of an agent-altitude spectral triple. Each Pack
# member's voice IS one agent_triple; the record names the (A, H, D)
# at the agent altitude plus the Bateson logical-type altitude at
# which the triple operates (per recognition #51 — mirror as
# expanding Hilbert space — different Pack voices operate at
# adjacent Bateson levels and the altitude field surfaces that
# explicitly).
#
# - peer       the typed Pack-member variant from the @pack
#              family-root (`| reed | mara | seam | glint | taut`);
#              substrate already named the typed-enum-discipline
#              precedent (the Seam-correction at C4/P1 tick 32 that
#              landed `peer` as a typed variant rather than bare ref).
# - algebra    A at the agent altitude — the operations the agent's
#              voice can perform. Per-agent species shards bind
#              this to the member's actual operational structure
#              (cf. pack/reed.mirror's relationship-witness-frame).
# - hilbert    H at the agent altitude — the space of utterances
#              the agent can produce.
# - dirac      D at the agent altitude — the kintsugi flow that
#              transforms input utterances to output.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple. Two
# agent_triples ARE the same triple iff all four fields are
# byte-equal under content-addressing.
type agent_triple = {
  peer:    peer,
  algebra: ref,
  hilbert: ref,
  dirac:   ref,
}

# === The handoff carrier ===
#
# Per the @pack family-root + per-agent shards + recognition #100
# §2.2-2.3 (turn + curvature_probe shape lifted to agent altitude):
# typed record over (source, target, content, tick). The substrate-
# architectural object naming one KK-cycle correspondence at Pack
# altitude.
#
# - source  : the agent_triple issuing the handoff
# - target  : the agent_triple receiving the handoff
# - content : the typed substrate-decl candidate the handoff carries
#             (typically a commit ref + the candidate it produces;
#             e.g., for today's cascade Turn 1, content = ref(a57a439))
# - tick    : the canonical substrate monotonic clock per
#             @epistemologic/reality/time (shards/epistemologic/
#             reality/time.mirror); handoffs compose only with
#             handoffs at strictly-greater tick (ordered cascade
#             discipline)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type handoff = {
  source:  agent_triple,
  target:  agent_triple,
  content: ref,
  tick:    tick,
}

# === The metalogue_thread carrier ===
#
# Per recognition #100 §2.4 (metalogue_session shape lifted to agent
# altitude): an ordered sequence of handoffs plus the thread's residual
# opacity. Same shape as @metalogue.metalogue_session and
# @facet/metalogue.metalogue_session and @spectral/metalogue.metalogue_session,
# lifted to the Pack altitude.
#
# - handoffs : the ordered sequence of agent-to-agent handoffs.
#              Turn-order matters per recognition #100 §2.5
#              altitude_consistency: reordering the cascade would
#              produce a structurally different thread (the
#              non-commutative [ω, ω] cross-term per §6.5).
# - opacity  : @glass transparency parameterized on handoff; every
#              unresolved gap (an agent's voice that couldn't fully
#              carry the handoff's substrate-pull content) is sited
#              on a specific handoff.
# - origin   : the agent_triple the thread is centered on (typically
#              the Pack member who opened the thread; for today's
#              cascade, origin = agent_voice(taut)).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type metalogue_thread = {
  handoffs: ref,                    # list of handoff; refines at species
  opacity:  transparency(handoff),
  origin:   agent_triple,
}

# === agent_voice action ===
#
# Per-agent voice realization: takes a Pack member (typed enum from
# the @pack family-root's peer carrier) and returns the agent_triple
# at that member's operational altitude. The substrate-vocabulary
# primitive for naming each voice as a spectral triple.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-agent species
# shards already declare the per-altitude (A, H, D) structure (cf.
# pack/reed.mirror's relationship-witness-frame; pack/mara.mirror's
# spec-writer-frame; etc.).
agent_voice(m: peer) -> agent_triple { \ }

# === compose_handoffs action ===
#
# KK-cycle composition at Pack altitude. Takes two handoffs h1, h2
# such that h1.target = h2.source (composability condition: the
# second handoff must originate from the agent the first handoff
# delivered to) and returns the composite handoff representing the
# two-step cascade.
#
# Non-commutative per recognition #100 §6.5 (the [ω, ω] cross-term):
# compose_handoffs(h1, h2) ≠ compose_handoffs(h2, h1) in general,
# because the substrate's curvature accumulates altitude-transition
# contributions in the order of composition. The orchestra's downbeat
# discipline (agreement-is-action) IS what makes composition
# well-defined under perturbation — each composition step honors the
# substrate-pull at the boundary.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual composite
# is computed by walking the substrate-decl content carriers and
# threading their refs.
compose_handoffs(h1: handoff, h2: handoff) -> handoff { \ }

# === handoff_well_typed predicate ===
#
# Mesland-correspondence verification at Pack altitude. Bilateral
# verdict (per recognition #37, Pask agreement) that a handoff
# h satisfies the KK-cycle correspondence conditions:
#
#   - h.source and h.target are well-formed agent_triples (their
#     refs resolve to (A, H, D) at the agent's altitude per their
#     per-agent shard)
#   - h.content's substrate-decl content is typed against both
#     source and target's algebras (the handoff carries content that
#     BOTH agents can read AS substrate-decl)
#   - the morphism semantics carry: target's reading of content IS
#     functorial over source's writing of content (no corruption in
#     transmission)
#
# Consumer shards (compose_handoffs above; forward-promised consumers
# at the per-agent altitude) name `requires handoff_well_typed(h)` to
# declare bilateral agreement that the handoff respects Mesland
# correspondence discipline.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary.
handoff_well_typed(h: handoff) -> verdict { \ }

# === pack_orchestra_coherent predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that a metalogue_thread composes coherently per
# Bateson conversation discipline. The thread IS coherent iff:
#
#   - Every adjacent pair (h_i, h_{i+1}) is composable
#     (h_i.target = h_{i+1}.source)
#   - Every handoff in the thread is handoff_well_typed
#   - The thread respects altitude_consistency (per recognition #100
#     §2.5): cross-altitude jumps differ by ±1 Bateson logical type
#     per handoff; multi-altitude jumps within one handoff are
#     forbidden
#   - The thread's substrate-pull descent is monotone: each handoff's
#     contribution composes to a total eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ descent across the
#     thread (Yang-Mills flow at Pack altitude per recognition #100
#     §6.5)
#
# Consumer shards (forward-promised) name `requires
# pack_orchestra_coherent(t)` to declare bilateral agreement that
# the thread IS a substrate-architecturally coherent metalogue session
# in the Mesland category at Pack altitude.
#
# Same shape as bilateral predicates the Pack family carries
# (pack_coherent, review_sound, spec_canonical, essay_grounds_corpus).
# This is the FIRST predicate at the Pack altitude that composes
# multiple handoffs into a thread verdict; per-agent predicates verify
# single agent contributions; pack_orchestra_coherent verifies the
# composed orchestra.
pack_orchestra_coherent(t: metalogue_thread) -> verdict { \ }

# === pack_metalogue_witnessing inheritance predicate ===
#
# Pask-agreement (recognition #37) bilateral commitment that a
# metalogue_thread IS a metalogue session in the Mesland category at
# Pack altitude. The bilateral commitment: the thread commits to
# carrying (handoffs, opacity, origin); the consumer commits to
# discharging handoff_well_typed across every handoff AND
# pack_orchestra_coherent on the composed thread AND pack_coherent
# on the underlying pack.
#
# Declared as a typed predicate so downstream species shards can
# write `requires pack_metalogue_witnessing(my_thread)` — same shape
# as `chirality_witnessing(c)` and `eigenform_witnessing(carrier)`
# at the cybernetic altitude. The predicate composes the per-handoff
# Mesland-correspondence discipline with the thread-level orchestra
# coherence discipline into one inheritance contract.
#
# Forward-promised inheritors:
#
# - @pack/metalogue/<member> (per-member metalogue refinements that
#   carry the member's voice-specific thread discipline; e.g., a
#   Mara-led thread inherits Mara's canonical-preservation discipline
#   on the handoffs Mara emits).
# - @spectral/metalogue (forward-promised cross-altitude lift via
#   recognition #100; each Pack metalogue_thread surfaces as one
#   curvature_probe at the spectral altitude when the Pack-runtime
#   composition lands).
pack_metalogue_witnessing(t: metalogue_thread) -> verdict { \ }

out @pack/metalogue
out agent_triple
out handoff
out metalogue_thread
out agent_voice
out compose_handoffs
out handoff_well_typed
out pack_orchestra_coherent
out pack_metalogue_witnessing
